{
  "note": "Sound and music (roadmap item 15; ui/play/sound.gd, checked by tools/check_data.gd). There are no recorded audio files: every sound is built in code from its description here, once, when first wanted. A sound is `wave` (sine, triangle, square, saw or noise), `notes` (one entry per step: a MIDI note number, 0 for a rest, or a list of numbers for a chord; 69 is the A above middle C), `step` (seconds per entry), `attack` and `release` (seconds each note takes to swell and to die away; together no longer than a step, so every note ends in silence and a looped track joins without a click), `volume` (0 to 1) and an optional `slide` (semitones each note bends by its end). `cues` play once; `tracks` loop and are built at `music_rate`, cues at `rate` (samples a second). `events` maps a battle event type from data/game/battle_events.json to a cue: a name, or `{cue, variants}` where the first variant whose `field` of the event equals `is` (true, false or text) gives the cue instead; an event not listed is silent. `results` maps how a fight ended to a cue, `stings` the succession and saga's-end screens, `screens` the title, a fight and the ended saga to a track (\"\" is silence), and `ages` lists the track of each Age of the world in turn (later Ages go round again). `levels` are the volume steps the menu offers, in decibels; sound effects and music each have their own and their own on or off, kept in settings.cfg, never the save. `voices` is how many cues can sound at once and `pitch_jitter` the share a cue's pitch may wander each time, for show. `limits` cap what the validator accepts, in seconds.",
